1
00:00:01,250 --> 00:00:05,405
Every deal. Every job. Every shipment.

2
00:00:05,445 --> 00:00:07,397
It all begins with a company.

3
00:00:07,487 --> 00:00:12,226
And every company has to prove it exists.
Again. And again.

4
00:00:12,826 --> 00:00:17,390
Karachi. Two a.m. Aisha built her product
in a week.

5
00:00:17,480 --> 00:00:19,507
Making it official will take months:

6
00:00:19,547 --> 00:00:23,055
the same checks, at every office, at every
bank.

7
00:00:23,102 --> 00:00:25,762
And at the next border, she starts again.

8
00:00:26,277 --> 00:00:30,458
In Abu Dhabi, Nadia approves new companies
for a free zone.

9
00:00:30,498 --> 00:00:36,595
Her systems don't talk to each other. So
she retypes. Re-checks. And waits.

10
00:00:37,110 --> 00:00:40,213
At the ministry, the economy arrives in
pieces.

11
00:00:40,253 --> 00:00:44,051
Dozens of systems. Every number, out of
date.

12
00:00:44,481 --> 00:00:47,558
Three people. One economy.

13
00:00:47,608 --> 00:00:51,101
Held back by systems that were never built
to talk to each other.

14
00:00:52,381 --> 00:00:55,436
What if a company only had to prove itself
once?

15
00:00:55,781 --> 00:01:00,264
One living record. Created in minutes.
Trusted everywhere.

16
00:01:00,694 --> 00:01:02,090
This is Mass.

17
00:01:03,820 --> 00:01:06,202
Aisha tells her agent what she's building.

18
00:01:08,042 --> 00:01:11,841
It prepares everything, and checks every
rule before filing.

19
00:01:13,301 --> 00:01:15,309
Nadia receives it complete. Nothing to
retype.

20
00:01:15,359 --> 00:01:19,979
Nothing to chase. She simply decides.

21
00:01:21,059 --> 00:01:23,999
Four minutes later, Aisha is in business.

22
00:01:25,269 --> 00:01:27,915
The ministry sees it happen, live.

23
00:01:28,433 --> 00:01:32,499
And when a rule changes, every company
gets it the same day.

24
00:01:33,769 --> 00:01:36,383
Every action is checked before it happens.

25
00:01:36,430 --> 00:01:41,781
At the base: the registry. Run by the
government, under its own keys.

26
00:01:41,914 --> 00:01:47,744
On top, the economy builds: licences,
banking, trade.

27
00:01:47,962 --> 00:01:53,637
And with a record every bank can trust,
trade finance flows from day one.

28
00:01:54,407 --> 00:01:56,731
Now imagine this across borders.

29
00:01:57,331 --> 00:02:03,010
When another nation joins, it recognises
the record. No starting over.

30
00:02:03,185 --> 00:02:09,956
Each keeps its own laws, its own data, its
own keys. Together: one economy.

31
00:02:10,556 --> 00:02:14,633
Formed. Licensed. Banked. Recognised.

32
00:02:15,233 --> 00:02:19,086
Mass. The operating system for sovereign
economies.

